<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<shacl>
	<id><![CDATA[ValidateHeight]]></id>
	<!--
		Explanation (SHACL):
		This SHACL shape validates the height of geometries against the highest wall.
		1. geom:IfcElementHeightShape targets every subject that has a geom:globalId (sh:targetSubjectsOf).
		2. A SPARQL-based constraint (sh:sparql) reads geom:globalId and geom:bboxMaxZ (the top
		   of the bounding box) of each target.
		3. A sub-query calculates ?globalMaxZ, the maximum geom:bboxMaxZ over all elements whose
		   rdf:type is ifc:IfcWall (the VALUES list can be extended with more IFC types).
		4. A target is reported as a violation when ?bboxMaxZ - ?globalMaxZ > 1, which means its top
		   is more than 1 unit above the highest wall.
		5. The result message is "Height violation for GlobalId=[...]: bboxMaxZ=... minus
		   globalMaxZ=... exceeds 1."
		6. The severity is sh:Violation.
	-->
	<shape uri="validate-height.ttl">
	</shape>
</shacl>